reset

## Coaxial line with a coated centre wire, from the ACE3P tutorial t3p/SIBC
## example. A quarter model: the two symmetry planes become magnetic boundaries,
## the wire an impedance boundary carrying the lossy coating, and the two end
## faces absorbing ports. Sideset IDs are what SIBC.t3p's ReferenceNumbers refer
## to, so do not renumber them without editing that file too.

create Cylinder height 1 radius 0.05
create Cylinder height 1 radius 0.1
sub 1 from 2
compress ids

webcut body 1 all plane with xplane
del body 2
webcut body 1 all plane with yplane
del body 1
compress ids

webcut body 1 all plane with zplane offset -0.25
webcut body 1 all plane with zplane offset  0.25

imprint body all
merge body all
compress ids

## The tutorial journal declares f/c and computes c/f/10 = 6 mm as a
## ten-points-per-wavelength guide, then meshes at 15 mm anyway. That literal is
## promoted to a real variable here so it is a sweepable knob; the value is
## unchanged, so this journal produces the tutorial's mesh.
#{f=5e9}
#{c=3e8}
#{wavelength_over_10 = c/f/10}
#{meshsize = 0.015}

vol all scheme tetmesh
vol all size {meshsize}

mesh vol all
block 1 vol 1 2 3

##sym. planes
sideset 1 surface with x_coord < 0.001
sideset 2 surface with y_coord < 0.001

##wire -- the lossy coated surface, monitored by 'wallossPower'
sideset 3 surface 13

##ports -- 4 is the excitation ('inputPower'), 5 the far end ('outputPower')
sideset 4 surface with z_coord < -0.49
sideset 5 surface with z_coord > 0.49

##exterior
sideset 6 surface 7 12 4 16 10

block all element type tetra10

export genesis "test-sibc.gen" overwrite
